    LLM: 'Game: Le Neuf. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Le Neuf ('Nines') is a French-Canadian trick-taking game from Quebec/Acadian communities. 3 players (4-player variant exists). 52-card deck, 13 each + 13-card 'Chômeur' spare hand. Start at 9 points, subtract to 0. Quota = 4 tricks: each trick above -1pt, below +1pt. Rotating trump cycle: Hearts-Diamonds-Clubs-Spades-No Trump. Can swap hand with Chômeur.",
    objective: 'Reach a score of zero by making more than your quota of four tricks per deal; each extra trick subtracts one point, each trick below quota adds one point.',
    gameplay: 'Rotating trumps: ♥-♦-♣-♠-NT cycle. May swap entire hand with Chômeur (first refusal passes right). Follow suit, trump if void. Quota=4 tricks: above=-1pt, below=+1pt. Win all 13=instant win (-9pts).',
